# SouqSmart – Quick Start Guide

> **Prerequisites**
> - Windows 10/11 with PowerShell or `cmd`.
> - Python 3.13 (the virtual environment already contains it).
> - Apache (XAMPP) installed at `C:\xampp` – used to serve the PHP product catalog.
> - Environment variables configured in `.env` (see `.env.example` for the required keys).

---

## 1. Verify the .env file

```text
# .env (example – copy from .env.example and edit values)
SOUQSMART_SERVICE_KEY=your_service_key
SOUQSMART_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key   # optional for LLM mode
SOUQSMART_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
SOUQSMART_GEMINI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3.5
SOUQSMART_INTENT_PARSER=deterministic   # use "llm" for Gemini mode
SOUQSMART_CATALOG_PROVIDER=php           # or "fixture" for local test data
SOUQSMART_PHP_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1/nice-shop
SOUQSMART_CATALOG_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3.0
```

Make sure the file **does not contain trailing spaces** and the values match your setup.

---

## 2. Start the PHP catalog (Apache)

```cmd
cd /d C:\xampp
apache\bin\httpd.exe
```

- If you see `Only one usage of each socket address ...` that means Apache is already running on port 80.  In that case you can skip this step.
- The catalog will be reachable at `http://127.0.0.1/nice-shop`.

---

## 3. Activate the Python virtual environment

```cmd
cd "D:\AI\souq smart"
.\.venv\Scripts\activate
```

You should see the prompt change to `(venv)`.

---

## 4. (Optional) Install / update dependencies

If you ever need to reinstall packages:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

The lockfile already contains all needed libraries (`fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `httpx`, `pydantic`, etc.).

---

