## 5. Run the FastAPI server

```cmd
uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

- The server starts in the foreground; you’ll see a line similar to:

INFO: Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000
 (Press CTRL+C to quit)

- **If you prefer it to stay in the background**, use:

```cmd
start /b uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000

6. Quick health‑check

Open a browser (or curl) and request:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/health

You should receive JSON like:

{
  "status": "ok",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "catalog_provider": "php",
  "llm": {
    "status": "disabled",                     // or "enabled"/"unconfigured" if LLM mode is on
    "provider": "gemini",
    "model": "gemini-3.8-flash",
    "configured": false,
    "usable": false
  }
}

If llm.status shows enabled and you have a valid Gemini API key, Gemini‑generated replies will be used for LLM‑enabled requests.
7. Run the test suite (optional but recommended)


pytest -q

All tests should pass (currently 66 passed).
If you want only the Phase‑3 acceptance tests:

pytest -q tests/test_phase3_repairs.py

8. Stopping the services
FastAPI: Press CTRL+C in the terminal where uvicorn is running.
Apache: Open a new terminal and run:

cd /d C:\xampp
apache\bin\httpd.exe -k stop

